  "description": "Established outbound TCP destinations observed on an ordinary developer workstation during a normal working session -- coding agents, a browser, a music client, a messaging client, a VPN agent and container tooling all running concurrently. Private, loopback, link-local, CGNAT and site-relay addresses are removed so no network topology is committed, and application names are not committed -- only a traffic class.",
  "capture_method": "Sockets and the cgroup-id -> process-name index were captured in a single pass, with the index taken immediately before AND after the netlink dump and unioned, so a short-lived scope cannot fall out between the two reads. Socket observations whose cgroup could not be resolved in either index were DROPPED rather than labelled, because an unlabelled row silently counted as non-inference would flatter the false-positive rate.",
  "label_method": "traffic_class is derived from process comm names co-resident in the socket's cgroup, most-specific-app-wins with browser taking precedence over coding-agent. This is a HEURISTIC oracle, not packet ground truth. A cgroup coarse enough to hold both a browser and a harness is labelled browser -- the conservative choice, since it can only increase the measured false-positive count, never decrease it. cgroup_has_harness and cgroup_has_browser are recorded separately so that mixed case stays auditable.",
  "ground_truth_rule": "A destination is a TRUE inference destination iff traffic_class == 'coding-agent'. Any destination the detector attributes to an inference provider while traffic_class != 'coding-agent' is counted a FALSE POSITIVE.",
