    {
      "destination": "160.79.104.10:443",
      "captured_traffic_class": "other-app",
      "actual": "Claude Code",
      "evidence": "The socket's cgroup (a systemd tmux-spawn scope) contains a process whose comm is 'node-MainThread' and whose /proc/<pid>/exe basename is 'node'. Claude Code is a Node binary, so the comm-based oracle -- which matches literal harness names such as 'claude' and 'agy' -- does not recognise it. 56,103,805 cumulative egress bytes were observed to this destination from that cgroup.",
      "why_not_corrected": "The captured label is deliberately left as recorded. Re-labelling a row after seeing which way it scores is how a measured rate quietly becomes an asserted one. The conservative figure (this row counted as a false positive) is the one reported.",
      "effect_on_measurement": "The shipped detector's measured false-positive rate of 1/12 is therefore an UPPER bound. The corrected rate is 0/12, but 0 is not claimed because this oracle cannot distinguish Claude Code from any other Node process without reading /proc/<pid>/cmdline, which is a prohibited entry."
    }
  ]
